## Static-method-with-args dispatch on stdlib type names.
##
## Regression probe for the historical codegen bug where
## `Thread.spawn_raw(closure)` (a `def self.X(arg)` lib decl on a
## stdlib class) would have a constant 0 prepended as the first
## argument at the call site, producing a verifier error
## "mismatched argument count … got 2, expected 1". The bug was
## resolved as a side-effect of commit 153e5c9 (module+mixin reshape
## touched the same MIR dispatch path). This fixture pins that the
## `def self.spawn_raw as "ruxen_thread_spawn"(closure: Int) -> Int`
## decl on `class Thread` dispatches without a phantom self — the
## next regression of that codepath fails here with a Cranelift
## verifier mismatched-argument-count error.
##
## The repro subject is `Thread.spawn_raw(closure)` — Int → Int, a
## `def self.X(arg)` shape that must dispatch WITHOUT a phantom `self` prepended.
##
## We round-trip a `String` through `.clone` afterwards as incidental coverage of
## the borrow→owned spelling: a bare literal `"42"` is ALREADY an owned `String`,
## and `owned.clone` deep-copies a borrow of it to a fresh owned `String`. (This
## used to be spelled `String.from(&owned)`, but the surface `String.from` static
## method was removed from the language — `clone` is the borrow→owned spelling.)

def main
  let closure = { || 42 }
  let handle = Thread.spawn_raw(closure)
  if handle == 0
    puts "spawn returned null"
  else
    let owned = "42"
    puts owned.clone
  end
end
